# 1. WORK CONTINUOUSLY THROUGH THE BLOCKERS

Do not stop merely because a prerequisite is missing if it can safely be installed, configured, discovered, or implemented from the current environment.

For each blocker:

```text
detect
→ safely resolve
→ verify
→ continue
```

Only stop when an action genuinely requires human authorization, billing approval, unavailable credentials, or an irreversible console decision that cannot safely be automated.

Do not stop because:

```text
Java is missing
Firebase CLI needs configuration
frontend config has not been copied yet
an emulator is not installed
a dependency needs installing
tests need to be written
```

Resolve those where possible.

