# 3. SOLVE THE JAVA / EMULATOR BLOCKER

The previous execution stopped because Java was unavailable.

Fix this.

Prefer:

```text
JDK 21
```

for new Firebase Emulator tooling.

Determine the operating system/package manager.

If Ubuntu/Debian and installation permissions exist, install an appropriate OpenJDK 21 package.

For example, conceptually:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install openjdk-21-jdk
```

Use the correct package for the detected system.

Then verify:

```bash
java -version
javac -version
```

Do not blindly run package-manager commands incompatible with the machine.

If sudo/install permission is genuinely unavailable:

1. report that exact blocker;
2. determine whether a user-local JDK installation is feasible;
3. use it if safely possible;
4. only then fall back to giving the maintainer the exact installation command.

Do not abandon all remaining implementation work just because Java cannot be installed.

