```

Use Firebase Authentication as the authoritative identity system.

The application must no longer bootstrap identity from:

```text
PostgreSQL sessions
express-session
__session
/api/auth/session legacy semantics
```

Use:

```javascript
onAuthStateChanged()
```

or the current appropriate Firebase mechanism.

The boot flow must become:

```text
page starts
↓
Firebase initializes
↓
auth state resolves
├─ user exists → application
├─ no user → authentication screen
└─ initialization error → recovery UI
```

There must never be an unexplained blank screen.

---

# 8. COMPLETE AUTHENTICATED API REQUESTS

Where Functions APIs remain appropriate, create one central authenticated request helper.

Conceptually:

```javascript
async function api(path, options = {}) {
    const user = auth.currentUser;

    if (!user) {
        throw new Error("Authentication required");
    }

    const token = await user.getIdToken();

    return fetch(path, {
        ...options,
        headers: {
            ...options.headers,
            Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`
        }
    });
}
```

Adapt this to the existing code.

Do not duplicate token logic across dozens of functions.

---

# 9. FUNCTIONS MUST VERIFY FIREBASE ID TOKENS

Confirm every protected server operation uses verified identity.

Expected conceptual flow:

```text
Authorization header
↓
Bearer token
↓
Firebase Admin verifyIdToken()
↓
decoded.uid
↓
authorization check
↓
operation
```

Never authorize using:

```text
req.body.userId
query-string userId
client ownerUid
client role
```

